# SubNation mobile — public runtime environment (Expo CNG).
#
# Copy to `.env` (git-ignored) or set via EAS build environment variables.
# Only EXPO_PUBLIC_* vars are inlined into the JS bundle at build time —
# NEVER put secrets here.

# ── API origin ────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# The backend the app talks to (the CSRF Origin shim sends this as the
# Origin header on every mutation — see src/lib/api.ts). Defaults to the
# production origin when unset; point it at your local/dev stack for
# device development.
EXPO_PUBLIC_API_URL=https://subnation.ly

# ── Firebase (Google sign-in) ────────────────────────────────────────────────
# The native Google sign-in lands with the owner's Firebase console config
# for ly.subnation.app (a follow-up round wires the firebase SDK +
# @react-native-google-signin). Until ALL FOUR values are present the
# login screen's Google button is hidden entirely (src/lib/firebase.ts
# isFirebaseAuthConfigured) — an honest absence instead of a dead button.
#
# Project settings → General → Your apps → the Android/iOS app:
EXPO_PUBLIC_FIREBASE_API_KEY=
EXPO_PUBLIC_FIREBASE_AUTH_DOMAIN=
EXPO_PUBLIC_FIREBASE_PROJECT_ID=
EXPO_PUBLIC_FIREBASE_APP_ID=

# ── Crash reporting (optional) ────────────────────────────────────────────────
# The mobile project's Sentry DSN; unset = the Sentry client stays disabled.
EXPO_PUBLIC_SENTRY_DSN=

# Crash reporting (FOLLOW-UP, R191): sentry-expo was REMOVED from v1 — the
# sentry-cocoa pod it pins fails the Xcode build on EAS's current toolchain
# ("std::allocator does not support const types", profiling-thread static
# assertions). Re-add it (pnpm exec expo install sentry-expo + the app.config
# plugin + the init block) once a sentry-expo release with a patched
# sentry-cocoa ships AND the owner creates the mobile Sentry project; the
# client init is DSN-gated (EXPO_PUBLIC_SENTRY_DSN — disabled when unset).
# EXPO_PUBLIC_SENTRY_DSN=
